flowchart TD
    start([Plan a release]) --> readBacklog[Read concept, current release scope and relevant feature definitions]
%% @airflow-context readBacklog
%% For a new release, read relevant approved backlog Definitions and the concept.
%% For replanning, also load the current scope, all its feature Definitions/statuses,
%% change findings and current evidence, including selected/implementing/verifying/
%% verified features. Existing membership is not lost because a feature left backlog.
%% Propose retained, added and removed IDs explicitly; unresolved or unapproved
%% Definitions cannot enter the approved scope. Preserve unaffected evidence with
%% impact rationale. Use goals, dependencies, priority and capacity, never tracker
%% order/status as approval. Do not select a feature belonging to another release.
%% @end-airflow-context
    readBacklog --> propose[Propose a coherent feature set for a version]
    propose --> draft[Save proposed scope draft for exact-version review]
    draft --> scopeApproval{User approves release scope?}
    scopeApproval -- No: revise proposed scope --> propose
    scopeApproval -- Defer release planning --> planningDeferred([Release planning deferred])
    scopeApproval -- Cancel release --> releaseCancelled([Release cancelled])
    scopeApproval -- Yes: record version and feature IDs --> scope[Write release scope in `.air/releases/1.2.0/scope.md`]
    scope --> scopeReady([Release scope approved])
%% @airflow-context scopeApproval
%% The human approves the exact version, included feature IDs, exclusions and
%% release goals. Bind the decision to the scope file digest. A changed set needs
%% a new scope approval. Deferring new planning leaves backlog unchanged;
%% deferring an existing release preserves its membership and valid evidence.
%% Record approval evidence in `.air/index.md` using the global instructions.

%% Feature transitions owned by this phase:
%% - `backlog` -> `selected`: Human approves inclusion in a release scope.
%% - `selected` / `implementing` / `verifying` / `verified` -> `backlog`: Human removes feature from scope or cancels release; Definition remains approved. Preserve historical evidence.

%% A feature belongs to at most one active release. Removing an unapproved feature
%% keeps it clarifying, deferred or rejected, never backlog. Release deferral keeps
%% membership and valid evidence; execution waits for explicit human reopening.

%% Release transition `planning -> scope-pending-approval`: Self-reviewed scope lists exact feature IDs and version; record_status becomes pending-approval. Owner: AI prepares and requests approval.

%% Release transition `scope-pending-approval -> scope-approved`: Scope digest is explicitly approved; append approval event. Owner: Human.

%% Release transition `deferred -> planning`: User explicitly reopens planning; revalidate the backlog and release goals. Owner: Human.
%% @end-airflow-context

    classDef boundary fill:#126a52,color:#ffffff,stroke:#126a52
    class start,scopeReady,planningDeferred,releaseCancelled boundary
    classDef approval fill:#fff0e8,color:#633b2c,stroke:#c68162
    class scopeApproval approval

%% @airflow-context propose
%% Record path: `.air/releases/<version>/scope.md`.
%% Record outline: Release goal; Included feature IDs; Excluded or deferred feature IDs; Dependencies and ordering; Release-level acceptance criteria.
%% Mutable statuses belong in the index. Example IDs and versions are placeholders.
%% @end-airflow-context
